cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LangAdapter, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LangAdapter"
abstract: >-
  LangAdapter gives a Python program one common interface to software
  projects in different programming languages. With the same calls, a
  program can read and edit a project's source code, check what the
  project's setup supports, and run its tests with coverage, mutation and
  timing measurements. Python, Java and C come with it, and it is built to be
  extended: a new language is one file with its adapter class, and code
  metrics and tool installers are added the same way, with no change to the
  library. LangAdapter needs no language model.
authors:
  - family-names: Kammler
    given-names: Kevin
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/k-kammler/langadapter"
keywords:
  - testing
  - test execution
  - coverage
  - mutation testing
  - pytest
  - junit
